 = = = The final years = = = 

 In 764 , he left Chengdu and returned to the capital , but he was not able to find a post . He spent the next few years wandering in the lower Yangtze region and the south of the Yangtze , and in 768 he moved to Kuizhou ( now Chongqing ) . He was still in Kuizhou when the Shuofang rebellion broke out in 765 . He was not able to return to the capital until 768 . He died in 770 in the province of Hunan . 

 = = = Legacy = = = 

 Du Fu 's poetry is known for its deep concern for the people and the country , and for its rich and varied style . His works are often seen as a reflection of the turmoil of the An Lushan rebellion and the decline of the Tang dynasty . He is often referred to as the " Poet Sage " ( Shīshèng ) , and his poetry is considered to be the " historical record of the poet " . 


