 Du Fu 's moral engagement is also a major theme of his poetry . He often wrote about the suffering of the people and the hardships of war , and he was also a strong advocate of Confucian ideals . He was a loyal official and a patriot . 

 Du Fu 's technical excellence is also a major theme of his poetry . He was a master of the regulated verse ( lüshi 律詩 ) and the ancient style ( gushī 古詩 ) . His poems are known for their dense use of allusion and their complex structure . 

