 = = = The An Lushan rebellion and the fall of the Tang = = = 

 In 755 , the An Lushan rebellion broke out . The rebellion began as a coup d 'etat by a general of mixed ethnic origin , An Lushan , who declared himself emperor of a short - lived state called Yan . The rebellion was a disaster for the Tang dynasty and for Du Fu . The capital Chang 'an fell to the rebels in 755 , and Du Fu was captured and held in the capital for three years . He managed to escape in 757 and made his way to the new imperial court in Lingwu ( now in Shanxi ) . There he was appointed as a minor official in the court of the newly enthroned Emperor Suzong . However , he was soon dismissed for his criticism of the emperor 's policies . 

