 Du Fu was born in 712 in the city of Qufu , in the province of Shandong . He was born into a family of scholars and officials , and his grandfather was a famous calligrapher and poet . His family had a long history of serving the government , and he was expected to follow in their footsteps . However , he was not successful in the imperial examinations , and he spent much of his life wandering and seeking official positions . 

 Du Fu 's early life was marked by a strong interest in poetry and literature . He was known for his talent and was influenced by the poetry of the previous generation , particularly the works of Li Bai . However , unlike Li Bai , who was more of a romantic and free-spirited poet , Du Fu was more concerned with the social and political issues of his time . 

 Du Fu 's life was also marked by the An Lushan Rebellion , which began in 755 and lasted until 763 . This rebellion had a profound impact on his life and work . He was forced to flee his home and spent much of his later years in a state of poverty and illness . Despite these hardships , he continued
