 Du Fu 's technical mastery is also reflected in his use of parallelism and antithesis . In classical Chinese poetry , parallelism ( 对仗 duìzhì ) is a common technique in which two phrases are structured in parallel , and antithesis ( 对偶 duìyǔ ) is a more specific form of parallelism in which the two phrases are in opposition . Du Fu 's use of these techniques is considered to be at the highest level . 

